Z||000006||MinnGreenGT||10-24-2001||08:39 PM||||I'd say it's an 86 'cause Cars & Concepts had to work on engineering the car at least 2 years before offering it as a factory option (for testing, etc...).  I was at the Cars & Concepts plant in Michigan (no longer called C&C, but still did GM's T-Tops) in the early 90's and got to see some of the pre-production T-Top work on the F-Bodies.  They had an assembly line complete Camaro, and a stripped T/A frame with the 1st T-Top installed sitting in their shop!  That was cool- also, my Dad got the last "offical factory installed T-Top" in his silver 88GT.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000007||T-top Fiero||10-24-2001||08:49 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by tomanyfieros:<BR><B>thats strange, why is it an 86 GT? 88's were the only ones that came with ttops.... not saying that it is not factory, i know my 87 GT is not factory ttoped because me and a friend put them in.... anyways, why is it an 86 GT? why cant it be an 88????   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_wtf.gif">  ?<BR>Jason<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>The C&C (aftermarket) T-top conversion for Fieros was available starting in 1984. It was available through C&C dealers around the country. This aftermarket conversion can be on any year Fiero, including the 88's. In the 88 model year you could order the C&C T-top conversion as a factory option.<P>Pat||||reg||1
